    <statement><p>Given <m>u(x,t)=\frac{1}{t^{3}}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}</m>, compute:</p>
<p><m>u_{xx}=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1}{t^{5}}x^{2}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}-\frac{1}{t^{4}}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>u_{x}=\frac{1}{t^{3}} \frac{\partial}{\partial{x}} e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}=-\frac{2x}{2t} \frac{1}{t^{3}} e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}=-\frac{1}{t^{4}}xe^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}</m>



We now differentiate <m>u_{x}</m> with respect to <m>x</m>, using the Product Rule and the Chain Rule.



<m>u_{xx}=-\left(\frac{1}{t^{4}}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}+\frac{1}{t^{4}}x\right) \frac{\partial}{\partial{x}} e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}=-\left(\frac{1}{t^{4}}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}+\frac{1}{t^{4}}x\right) \cdot -\frac{2x}{2t} e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}=\frac{1}{t^{5}}x^{2}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}-\frac{1}{t^{4}}e^{-\frac{x^{2}}{2t}}</m>





</solution>
